  "version": 1,
  "note": "How the Q and E moves look (the move effects, Matt, October 27, 2026: real light on the cave, moths that look like moths, all twelve moves). Read by src/world/hollow/move-fx.js; loaded on tool pages only (tools/move-arena.html, tools/move-fx-lab.html) until H3. Four building blocks: lights (real point lights on the floor, walls, walker and foes: col is linear light, the lantern is about 1.4; reachM how far it falls; lifeS how long; curve: flash (bright then fading), hold (steady then fading over the last fadeS), pulse; flicker 0..1), sparks (glowing points: n, speed and up in m/s as [min, max], lifeS, size in m, col, gravity m/s2 (negative rises), drag per s, stretch: seconds of motion the streak shows, spread: how far round they go in degrees), threads (glowing strands) and moths. Floor marks (col drawn as unlit light) grow in over growS and fade over their life. Every colour is linear light, so the palette at the tonemap still has the last word. The cinematic pass (November 3, 2026) adds: sparks may bounce (the share of their fall kept on hitting the floor) with friction (what they keep of their slide), cool (the colour they cool to over their life, an ember lying on the floor) or be dust (a lit, soft, non-glowing puff: col is its albedo, shaded by the lights); lights may cast shadows (shadow: soft shadows of the walker, the things and the pillars, recipes/world/hollow-cine.json shadows); the gathers in the wind-ups (a flame or seed in the hand, sparks drawn into the lantern, dust lifting, motes rising), Groundline's slam and its crack cooling over crack.lifeS, the scorch's ember rim, and the swing's contact (chips, dust and a small light at the body, scaled by glanceShare and breakShare).",
